In rec.games.hack you write:

>If anyone can get PYEC's, Hearts of Ahriman, Sceptres of Might,
>doesn't that kind of diminish the Uniqueness of each item?
>Could we possibly make all these artifacts off limits for wishes
>(except for the Wizard mode, of course).

I can agree with this.

>I also was led to wonder about wishing for the other Artifacts
>in the game, many of which have implicit alignments.  I would think
>that a Lawful God would never hand out Stormbringer, etc.

Note that wishes are NOT granted by your god, but by genies, ghosts,
deamons, wands, etc... You'll never get Stormbringer by praying, unless
you're chaotic.

>I was then led to consider the following proposal for granting
>artifacts for wishes:

>    demons     chaotic only
>    djinni     neutral only
>    thrones    lawful only (unless they are demon thrones)
>    WOW        anything -- but your God will listen in
>               bad thing for a Knight to wish for Stormbringer....

The idea in itself is supported wholeheartedly! I don't know about
djinnies and thrones, though. I see why you include these (to get one
chaotic, one neutral, and one lawful), but I don't see why djinnies
would be neutral and thrones lawful.

Anyone know what the alignment of a djinni in ADND is? I know it's
opposite to the Efreeti, but I can't recall what's what (who's what).

B.t.w., I think that your God should ALWAYS listen in, not only when
using a WOW. Talking about a WoW: I think NetHack, like Moria and ADND,
should have the infamous Wand of Wonder (the wand that reproduces
random other wand effects: they should have the same chance as the
corresponding wands have of appearing).


